92 tunnel \u2192 example app does *not* go through the iPhone, so it works fine in isolation (smoke test step 2 \u2713). The forward leg, which *does* go through the iPhone, breaks on every press where the WS happened to be dead.\n\n## Workarounds, ordered by effort\n\n1. **Force a fresh WS, then press immediately.** Quit the MentraOS Manager app on your iPhone (swipe up), reopen, wait until the cloud log prints `Glasses WebSocket connection opened`, then take the photo within 30\u201360 s. Photos work until the next idle stretch puts the WS back to sleep. This is the zero-code workaround you want for now.\n\n2. **Keep the iPhone screen alive while testing.** Lock screen \u2192 enable AssistiveTouch + plug it in, or just open the MentraOS Manager UI and keep your finger awake. The WS doesn't go zombie if iOS doesn't suspend the JS thread.\n\n3. **Hide the symptom (not the bug) by using a custom webhook.** In your example app's [PhotoManager.ts:71-78](MentraOS-Camera-Example-App/src/server/manager/PhotoManager.ts#L71-L78), pass `customWebhookUrl: ${process.env.PUBLIC_URL}/photo-upload` into `session.camera.requestPhoto({...})`. When the cloud sees `customWebhookUrl` it resolves your SDK promise immediately ([PhotoManager.ts:199-215](cloud/packages/cloud/src/services/session/PhotoManager.ts#L199-L215)) instead of waiting 30 s for an upload \u2014 so the user-facing \"Photo request timed out\" message goes away. The photo still won't actually arrive when the WS is dead, but at least the example app doesn't sit there for 30 s on every press. Use this if the demo is more important than the underlying flow.\n\n4. **Real fix (cloud-side, ~5 lines).** Tighten the cloud's glasses-WS heartbeat in [bun-websocket.ts](cloud/packages/cloud/src/services/websocket/bun-websocket.ts) so it sends a ping every ~15 s and force-closes if no pong comes back inside 30 s. Right now the cloud's WS health monitor (per `cloud/AGENTS.md` \"Connection Health Monitoring\") is too lenient \u2014 a